  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NESA/AFRICOM Workshop 01-24: &quot;The Impact of the Changing Nature of Security on the Region&quot;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The group will examine theoretical threats and how best to develop capabilities and strategies to address new technologies, insurgency and hybrid conflicts, and non-traditional security demands. Discussions will include challenges that range from cyber, anti-access, criminal elements to transnational, malign players, and the super-empowered non-state actors. Lastly, the group will look at the impact of grey/hybrid warfare and the convergence of technologies that directly impact how we organize, how we fight and more importantly what we can expect from enemy states, as well as non-state actors. The objective is to lay out the extent of the problem, but more importantly address existing initiatives taken nationally and regionally and propose new regional initiatives with inputs/insights from &quot;whole of government&quot; and &quot;whole of society&quot; in a venue for USAFRICOM, senior security professionals, and young security experts to discuss security requirements, protocols, processes and policies to address/brainstorm required institutional, organizational, and cultural changes under Chatham House rule of non-attribution.</narrative>
  </description>
